<http://data.silknow.org/event/829b7cc5-14fa-348e-b92a-344cdb377519>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Bequeathed by Lady Henriques, the acquisition recorded in Registered File 53/986 (on Nominal File MA/1/H1634). The writing table came from Normandy Park, near Guildford, Surrey, where Lady Henriques had a collection of furniture made between 1790 and 1820, including a number of pieces in satinwood. She was the widow of Sir Philip Gutterez Henriques (1867-1950), a barrister and civil servant.  Their only son, Philip, was killed in action in 1815, and from 1930, Lady Henriques had been seeking to make bequests to the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford and the V&amp;A of pieces from her collection. \n\nOn loan to Preston Hall, Stockton on Tees, 1955-2008."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6592ea9-4902-33a9-90d7-c9d654d48d84> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Bequeathed by Lady Henriques, the acquisition recorded in Registered File 53/986 (on Nominal File MA/1/H1634). The writing table came from Normandy Park, near Guildford, Surrey, where Lady Henriques had a collection of furniture made between 1790 and 1820, including a number of pieces in satinwood. She was the widow of Sir Philip Gutterez Henriques (1867-1950), a barrister and civil servant.  Their only son, Philip, was killed in action in 1815, and from 1930, Lady Henriques had been seeking to make bequests to the Ashmolean Museum, Oxford and the V&amp;A of pieces from her collection. \n\nOn loan to Preston Hall, Stockton on Tees, 1955-2008."@en .

